346
00:22:21,670 --> 00:22:25,610
So when looking at delta, there are basically five scenarios when it comes to delta in a bar.

347
00:22:25,810 --> 00:22:27,700
It could be extremely positive number

348
00:22:27,700 --> 00:22:30,220
indicates aggressive buyers have dominated the bar. Buyers

349
00:22:30,220 --> 00:22:34,630
are buying all the available supply offered by sellers and moving the market higher.

350
00:22:34,630 --> 00:22:41,590
What I mean by extremely positive delta, usually it's something, you know, over 1,000 or more.

351
00:22:43,110 --> 00:22:45,839
Average positive delta number would indicate aggressive buyers

352
00:22:45,839 --> 00:22:48,568
outnumber the sellers, but not overwhelmingly. This can

353
00:22:48,568 --> 00:22:54,368
be a sign of accumulation when a series of average positive delta bars are being put together.

354
00:22:55,690 --> 00:22:57,662
You know, for example, it depends

355
00:22:57,662 --> 00:22:59,634
on. You should know what sort

356
00:22:59,634 --> 00:23:03,908
of deltas you'll see in your normal market, depending on what you trade.

357
00:23:04,630 --> 00:23:16,570
You know, for the E-minis, usually when you see deltas over 5,000 or 6,000, you know, that's an extremely positive delta number.

358
00:23:17,070 --> 00:23:19,688
When you see things, you know, delta is

359
00:23:19,688 --> 00:23:21,324
around 1,000, you know, 900, 1,000, anywhere between

360
00:23:21,324 --> 00:23:28,852
500 and 1,500. It's kind of an average positive delta number. It's just telling you there was slightly more buying than selling in the bar.

361
00:23:31,390 --> 00:23:33,955
A small or negative delta number that's close

362
00:23:33,955 --> 00:23:35,878
to zero indicates aggressive buyers and

363
00:23:35,878 --> 00:23:41,649
sellers are pretty much evenly matched. Prices at equilibrium, both buyers and sellers are happy to trade at.

364
00:23:41,650 --> 00:23:44,320
You know, what I consider that is,

365
00:23:44,320 --> 00:23:46,609
you know, a number less than 100,

366
00:23:46,609 --> 00:23:51,187
either positive or negative, because, you know, as I said, it's rare.

367
00:23:51,770 --> 00:23:54,672
You do get zero deltas in a bar

368
00:23:54,672 --> 00:23:57,212
where it's perfectly matched, but, you know,

369
00:23:57,212 --> 00:24:00,840
sometimes you're going to get a delta of 6 or 30 or 87.

370
00:24:01,930 --> 00:24:04,137
You know, especially when the bar has,

371
00:24:04,137 --> 00:24:06,344
you know, a total volume of, say, 8,000

372
00:24:06,344 --> 00:24:09,497
lots that trade in and the delta is, you know, 70.

373
00:24:10,770 --> 00:24:15,750
You know, it's telling you that, you know, the buying and selling is evenly matched.

374
00:24:16,510 --> 00:24:18,780
You know, I tend to take it, whether

375
00:24:18,780 --> 00:24:20,766
it's positive or negative, in the same

376
00:24:20,766 --> 00:24:23,888
light, you know, sort of treat it as a neutral delta.

377
00:24:23,890 --> 00:24:31,170
So, an average negative delta number indicates aggressive sellers outnumber the aggressive buyers.

378
00:24:31,570 --> 00:24:36,310
Not overwhelmingly, you know, it can be a sign of steady reduction of position or shorts building up.

379
00:24:36,710 --> 00:24:39,162
An average negative delta number would be

380
00:24:39,162 --> 00:24:41,614
something, you know, minus 500 to, you know,

381
00:24:41,614 --> 00:24:45,467
minus 1,500, just as an average positive delta would be around 500 to 1,500.

382
00:24:47,790 --> 00:24:51,136
An extremely negative delta number indicates aggressive sellers have dominated

383
00:24:51,136 --> 00:24:53,813
the bar. Our sellers are basically hitting every

384
00:24:53,813 --> 00:24:57,829
